Hi Apurva,
While I'm not familiar with standard practices in this area of research, I should say that we use 5 x 10^-8 as our threshold for genome-wide discovery. But if we are estimating model parameters for no-SNP models, we just use the standard p<.05 threshold, potentially with a Bonferonni correction if there is a family of tests.
All the best,
Elliot

